I propose that adopting a visible, documented tracking system will eliminate ambiguity regarding chore assignments. This assumes that the roommates are willing to agree to a formal structure and that the avoiding friend's withdrawal is a reaction to conflict rather than a fundamental refusal to contribute. A proposed test for this approach would be a two-week trial of a shared chart; if arguments persist despite clear documentation, the problem is likely rooted in interpersonal resentment rather than organizational failure.